<section id="control" class="ns-section ns-control" aria-labelledby="control-title">
  <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
    <header class="ns-section-heading">
      <h2 id="control-title" class="t-heading">What control means</h2>
      <p class="ns-lead">You can say what the agent does in one breath: it can read this inbox, look up these records and prepare a reply, and it needs approval before it sends a quote.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="ns-prose">
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A defined job.</strong> One piece of work, written down, with a test for whether it was done right.</li>
        <li><strong>Named limits.</strong> The agent can reach only the inboxes, folders and systems we list.</li>
        <li><strong>A person approves.</strong> The agent drafts and prepares. Anything sent to a customer or changed in your records waits for a person.</li>
        <li><strong>A record.</strong> Every run is logged where you can read it.</li>
        <li><strong>Your accounts and keys.</strong> The AI model is used through a business account in your name, and I hold nothing you cannot revoke.</li>
        <li><strong>Where it runs is your choice.</strong> Either the model vendor's hosted service under your account, or a server you own, rented in your own hosting account.</li>
        <li><strong>If we stop working together, you keep everything and it keeps running.</strong> The accounts, keys, configuration and notes are yours.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 class="t-heading">What it is not</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>This is not offline. When the agent uses the AI model, the text it is working on is sent to the model provider.</li>
        <li>A server you own needs updates, backups and someone watching it.</li>
        <li>AI is used only where something has to be read and interpreted, alongside your existing software and ordinary automation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If the agent is down, the work waits in a queue and your team can do it the old way.</p>
      <p><%= link_to "Where your agent runs", studio_where_agents_run_path, class: "ns-text-link" %></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
